   "id": "trap",
   "title": "The bait on the Pratzen",
   "time": "1 December, evening",
   "narrative": "Napoleon has pulled his troops off the Pratzen Heights and let the Allies see a thin, nervous right wing near the Goldbach villages. Most of his army hides in the dead ground west of the Bosenitz, between Puntowitz and Girzikowitz, while Davout's corps hurries up from Vienna. The Allies, pressed by the Tsar's circle and following Weyrother's plan, camp on and east of the Pratzen, ready to swing south and roll up the French right.",
