   "id": "telnitz",
   "title": "Allied columns strike Telnitz",
   "time": "c. 08:00",
   "narrative": "The Allied left wing marches down the Pratzen's southern slopes and hits Telnitz, held by the 3rd Line. Austrian and Russian assaults throw the French out, but the first of Davout's men arrive from the south, retake the village, and are in turn driven off by hussar charges. French guns across the Goldbach hold the Allies in check. The attack comes slower and more tangled than Weyrother intended, since Liechtenstein's cavalry crossing the line delays a column.",
